{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\dfrac1x\\sin(x)$ is the product of two, more basic, expressions: $\\dfrac1x$ and $\\sin(x)$.\n\nTherefore, $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ can be found using **the product rule**:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)v(x)]\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)]v(x)+u(x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}[v(x)]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=u'(x)v(x)+u(x)v'(x)\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac1x\\sin(x)\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac1x\\right)\\sin(x)+\\dfrac1x\\dfrac{d}{dx}(\\sin(x))\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{The product rule}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(x^{-1}\\right)\\sin(x)+\\dfrac1x\\dfrac{d}{dx}(\\sin(x))\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Write } \\dfrac1x\\text{as a power}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-1x^{-2}\\cdot \\sin(x)+\\dfrac1x\\cdot \\cos(x)\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Differentiate }x^{-1}\\text{ and }\\sin(x)}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{\\cos(x)}{x}-\\dfrac{\\sin(x)}{x^2}\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Simplify}}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{\\cos(x)}{x}-\\dfrac{\\sin(x)}{x^2}$\n\nor any other equivalent form.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $y=\\dfrac1x\\sin(x)$.\n\n$\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=$ [[☃ expression 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"\\frac{x\\cos\\left(x\\right)-\\sin\\left(x\\right)}{x^2}"}],"buttonSets":["basic","trig","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
